{"change_summary":"Added explicit oxygen-budget provenance tracking through `BudgetEntry`/`TickBudgetRecord`, tightened `assert_o2_balanced` so it rejects snapshot-only bookkeeping for gross-O2 stages, and introduced a shared debug-env lock plus `with_budget_debug_env()` so `TANK_BUDGET_DEBUG` no longer leaks across parallel tests. I also added regressions that lock in bidirectional dissolved-oxygen gross accounting and the new helper failure mode for snapshot-only `system:dissolved_oxygen` entries.","outstanding_risks":["`cargo test -p tank_core` still hits an unrelated failure in `crates/tank_core/tests/water_change_mass_balance.rs::water_change_50_percent_ro_like_halves_dissolved_totals`, which appears to come from concurrent water-change/carbonate work already present in the worktree.","The explicit-O2-stage guard is intentionally label-based (`system:dissolved_oxygen` and `action:water_change` today); any future bidirectional oxygen stage must be added to that allowlist or the helper will not enforce explicit gross bookkeeping for it.","The worktree still contains unrelated tracked edits in other files plus the pre-existing untracked `.ralph-burning/` directory, which I left untouched."],"steps":[{"description":"Inspected the budget helper, budget-recording path, and debug-env test harness to confirm the two pending gaps: oxygen gross bookkeeping could regress to snapshot-only accounting, and `TANK_BUDGET_DEBUG` could leak across parallel tests.","order":1,"status":"completed"},{"description":"Patched budget recording to carry `BudgetRecordingKind`, updated `assert_o2_balanced` to reject snapshot-only accounting for gross-O2 stages, and added a shared lock-backed `with_budget_debug_env()` path so `step_and_inspect()` and the smoke test serialize debug-env access.","order":2,"status":"completed"},{"description":"Added regression coverage for explicit dissolved-oxygen gross in/out bookkeeping and for helper rejection of snapshot-only `system:dissolved_oxygen` entries, then ran formatting, targeted tests, a `--nocapture` leak check, clippy, and a full `tank_core` suite pass up to the unrelated existing water-change failure.","order":3,"status":"completed"}],"validation_evidence":["`cargo fmt --all` passed.","`cargo test -p tank_core --test budget_helpers --test dissolved_oxygen --lib` passed.","`cargo test -p tank_core --test budget_helpers -- --nocapture` passed; only the expected debug-output smoke-test block and the intentionally caught panic from the new snapshot-only O2 regression test were emitted, with no stray debug blocks from unrelated tests.","`cargo clippy -p tank_core -- -D warnings` passed.","`cargo test -p tank_core` ran through the updated budget-helper, dissolved-oxygen, engine, budget-tracking, save-load, shrimp, and validation suites successfully, then failed only at the unrelated `water_change_mass_balance` regression noted above."]}